WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.613 --> 00:00:05.700
- They have destroyed that masjid

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.185
and that is a wrong thing.

00:00:07.185 --> 00:00:08.018
- Yeah.

00:00:08.018 --> 00:00:09.700
- But do you know how many temples

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.340
in Kashmir have they burnt?

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.710
350 temples.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.607
- Are we settling scores?

00:00:13.607 --> 00:00:15.107
- No.
- Exactly.

00:00:15.107 --> 00:00:16.270
- Hindus and Muslims

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.149
are like the Montagues
and Capulets of India.

00:00:18.149 --> 00:00:20.023
We've been waring for centuries.

00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:24.155
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.060
- [Interviewer] Growing Up,

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.000
I was taught to stay
away from the other side.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.303
Can the agreers please step forward?

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.360
- It wasn't said so strongly,

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.411
(both chuckle)
nothing really did.

00:00:54.411 --> 00:00:58.050
There was generally a non-appreciation

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.130
of me hanging out with Hindu friends.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.270
So there was not a clear thing

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.610
that don't hang out with Hindus,

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:05.787
but discouraging.

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:07.120
Where are you going?

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.953
He's a Hindu.

00:01:07.953 --> 00:01:10.920
You don't even know how
they would have coped.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.110
Why are you going to their
birthday party or something?

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.750
Whereas if I have a Muslim friend,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.960
he was somewhat more welcome.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.730
- So yeah, in my family

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.900
I think I have actually seen my parents

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.950
neglect a lot of my Muslim friends

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.970
and very sternly my mother
specifically walk up to me

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.300
and tell me that don't make Muslim friends

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.590
or whenever there was a
Muslim friend's birthday party

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:36.648
she would tell me not to go there.

00:01:36.648 --> 00:01:38.982
So there was this very cold environment.

00:01:38.982 --> 00:01:42.200
Like I would see my mother
not treating them very well,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.180
not sitting with them

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.380
or trying to even initiate a discussion.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.670
It really needs to be stopped.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:51.160
You can't let your kids grow
in such a venomous environment

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.981
that it ultimately takes a toll on them.

00:01:52.981 --> 00:01:54.200
And when they grow up,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.718
they start just hating the other
community to such an extent

00:01:57.718 --> 00:02:00.929
that they can't even engage
in discussions with them.

00:02:00.929 --> 00:02:04.439
- [Interviewer] Can we have
the disagreers come forward?

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:06.527
(footsteps thudding)

00:02:06.527 --> 00:02:08.840
- My experience was quite the opposite.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.916
In my house, actually my
sister's best friend was Muslim

00:02:11.916 --> 00:02:13.880
and she used to live in our colony.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.955
And for every Diwali,

00:02:14.955 --> 00:02:16.996
it's like she didn't have
anywhere to go or anything to do.

00:02:16.996 --> 00:02:19.250
So she used to spend Diwali with us.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.090
So my family's been very accepting.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.830
- So for my parents, it was never a choice

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.750
because most of my
friends were Muslims only-

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.583
- Same.

00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:31.390
- So there was no choice for
them to stop me somewhere.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.957
But yes, it was communicated (indistinct),

00:02:35.724 --> 00:02:37.850
never marry outside your...

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.700
- What I really enjoy whenever someone

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.620
from a different religion
would come to the house,

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.730
then the level of curiosity
that my parents would have.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:46.563
- Absolutely.
(all chuckle)

00:02:46.563 --> 00:02:49.860
- And that's also something
very bad about our society.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.240
After 1000 years of coexistence,
there is still curiosity.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.330
How dumb are we?

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.163
- [All] Yeah.

00:02:55.163 --> 00:02:57.820
- Like you still don't know
about the other person.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.960
(suspense music)

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.993
- I've been married to a Muslim boy

00:03:00.993 --> 00:03:02.131
by my own will and choice,

00:03:02.131 --> 00:03:04.290
of course, against my parents will.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.560
They still don't speak
to my husband at all.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.440
They have cordial relations with me,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.660
which I think I've over the time

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.820
come to accept that it's okay

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.180
if they don't want to talk to him,

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:16.404
it's their decision at the end of the day

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:18.412
and I need to respect it.

00:03:18.412 --> 00:03:21.062
- [Interviewer] Someone I know has died

00:03:21.062 --> 00:03:22.783
because of this conflict.

00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:28.290
(footstep thudding)

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.233
- We being Kashmir Pandits,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.393
are treated as a minority
community in Jammu and Kashmir.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:40.093
And because of this religious extremism,

00:03:44.086 --> 00:03:46.000
my father was assassinated

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.250
when I was at the age of 15 or 16.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.650
All house was coordinated by militants.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.520
And he was taken from that my place.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.850
And he was assassinated.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.380
Because of this religious conflict,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.823
certain innocents are being targeted.

00:04:07.394 --> 00:04:10.557
And if the extremism and
conflicts will go on,

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.383
such things will happen.

00:04:15.034 --> 00:04:18.117
(footsteps thudding)

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.227
- I think a lot of us (chuckles),

00:04:28.227 --> 00:04:29.140
- Yeah.
- Are just tongue-tied

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:29.973
for now.

00:04:31.535 --> 00:04:32.368
But if I may,

00:04:32.368 --> 00:04:35.670
I think I just have had
a lot of respect for you,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.510
like right now

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.680
because I think it takes a lot

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.660
to be a firsthand victim of a crime

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.980
and then still not develop that hatred

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.230
and let that hatred get so much to you

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.577
that you start blaming an
entire community for it.

00:04:49.577 --> 00:04:52.630
Because at the end you have
to realize that an individual

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.060
or few individuals
belonging to that community

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.800
were actually responsible for it

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.170
and not the entire community.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.260
So I think if we actually
had people like you

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.542
who were so practical and understanding,

00:05:02.542 --> 00:05:05.700
we wouldn't be in this
situation we are in today.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.330
- No, that's actually very true.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.400
I've spent a lot of time
in Jammu and Kashmir.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.390
My father was in the army,

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.550
we were posted there for a long time.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.196
I've seen a lot of terrorism

00:05:14.196 --> 00:05:16.260
and a lot of violence in front of me.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.990
We didn't go to school for
many months because of that

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.230
so I've lost out big
chunks of my childhood.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.063
Initially, when you'd introduce yourself

00:05:22.063 --> 00:05:24.030
and you said you were a Kashmir Pandit,

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.430
I was immediately filled with fear

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.100
because I've had a lot of negativity

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:34.100
from people who tend to
harbor hate against people

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.380
with literally just my
surname, for of course,

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.281
things that have happened
terrible in their lives.

00:05:39.281 --> 00:05:41.403
- [Pallavi] Yeah, absolutely.

00:05:41.403 --> 00:05:44.280
- But to see somebody
emerge from such a situation

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.570
and then still come out the other side

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.761
with the level of maturity

00:05:47.761 --> 00:05:50.820
that you are able to show right now,

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.356
it's really incredible to see yeah.

00:05:52.356 --> 00:05:53.920
- What you have been through,

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.890
given that despite that personal tragedy,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:06:00.010
you have managed to keep
yourself just and fair,

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.003
my salute to you.

00:06:02.936 --> 00:06:05.453
And if it matters, I doubt it does,

00:06:06.877 --> 00:06:08.350
but as a part of a Muslim community,

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.850
I am terribly sorry for your loss.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.348
- See, that's the problem.

00:06:11.348 --> 00:06:13.354
I mean, you can be sorry to him.

00:06:13.354 --> 00:06:15.685
Why do you have to take the blame for it?

00:06:15.685 --> 00:06:16.767
- [Both] Exactly.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.580
- That is something
that I don't understand.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.622
None of my business, not my problem.

00:06:20.622 --> 00:06:21.940
Some people did it,

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.170
I am the representative for myself.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.568
That doesn't make me absolute,

00:06:26.568 --> 00:06:28.780
in the sense to represent
that entire culture.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.450
It's just a tiny facet.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.290
- It does.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.760
- No. You know actually-
- Why.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.320
- When you start being apologetic
for the entire community

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.170
is actually when you start
giving the other side

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.774
the chance to blame the entire community.

00:06:41.774 --> 00:06:43.005
- Pallavi, made a point.

00:06:43.005 --> 00:06:46.550
So she said that if
everybody was like him,

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.090
we wouldn't be here at all.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.350
But I wanna just take to the other side

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.240
because to go what he has gone through,

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.120
I believe the pain would be immense.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.722
And if that means that
I lash out at society

00:06:57.722 --> 00:07:01.880
and the perpetrators, at whoever
or whatever was responsible

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.090
I believe that there is
hope for understanding

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.517
those kind of violent actions.

00:07:06.517 --> 00:07:08.080
- Oh, absolutely not.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.675
I so disagree with that point of view.

00:07:09.675 --> 00:07:12.890
We'd be living in an
uncivilized and lawless society

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:15.260
if we actually start
propagating thoughts like this,

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.950
that being violent is okay at a point.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.589
Your aggression, your being
upset at the situation,

00:07:21.589 --> 00:07:23.760
the immense pain that you have felt,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.410
I'm sure people are going to understand.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.296
But saying that it's justified
for me to be violent-

00:07:28.296 --> 00:07:29.558
- I'm not saying it's justified-

00:07:29.558 --> 00:07:31.500
- I think that's wrong.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.750
- If I understand what he's trying to say,

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.350
is if he goes out

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.800
because his family was
subjected to violence

00:07:38.995 --> 00:07:40.835
and he killed somebody,

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:44.010
what he's saying actually
that killing somebody is bad,

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.030
that is not a justification for killing.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:46.863
But probably what he's saying

00:07:46.863 --> 00:07:49.550
is that when it comes to punishing him,

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:50.383
- Yeah.

00:07:50.383 --> 00:07:52.294
- The history which existed.

00:07:52.294 --> 00:07:55.490
So that should serve as not
a defense against his crime,

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.323
but a mitigating circumstance.

00:07:56.323 --> 00:07:57.156
- [Pallavi] No, but
then I have a question-

00:07:57.156 --> 00:07:59.271
- This guy understands me so well.

00:07:59.271 --> 00:08:00.104
(Zarah laughs)

00:08:00.104 --> 00:08:01.060
- How's that gonna change anything?

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:01.893
- [Pallavi] Exactly.

00:08:01.893 --> 00:08:02.930
- I think that's the middle ground.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.547
- Then how does that make him different

00:08:04.547 --> 00:08:07.448
from the people who
assassinated his father?

00:08:07.448 --> 00:08:09.550
How does that make him different then?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.099
- See, what Pallavi is saying is that-

00:08:11.099 --> 00:08:13.108
- Because he also went
ahead and shot those people.

00:08:13.108 --> 00:08:14.827
Those people shot his father.
- Blaming an entire community

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:17.820
is not an answer to that.
- So where is the difference?

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.400
- We can justify by
doing through individuals

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.540
but blaming up complete
community is not justified,

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.310
so that is what Pallavi,

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.470
and I also agree on that.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.920
Muslims and Hindus can bridge those gaps

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.090
because there are some negative energies

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.930
which will pull you in your way,

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.430
but we need to be tolerant.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.410
We need to be very much patient

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.369
about the actions which we are doing.

00:08:42.369 --> 00:08:45.294
- [Interviewer] The government
has created more divide

00:08:45.294 --> 00:08:47.633
between Hindus and Muslims.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.373
- Yeah.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:54.423
- Really? Are you guys not coming forward?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.160
- So I think of course you
have reports after reports.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.530
In fact there is a New York Times post

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.783
that has clearly said and I quote,

00:09:05.783 --> 00:09:09.180
" that the data of hate crime in India

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.310
gets released based on who the hater is."

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.750
So when the government of India

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.720
decides to release a data
on hate crimes in India

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:22.490
and it excludes lynchings of minorities

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.909
and only puts forward certain facts

00:09:24.909 --> 00:09:27.050
where the majority is favored,

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.370
crimes against majority.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.990
I think of course the government
has a huge agenda to solve

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:33.368
in pleasing the majority.

00:09:33.368 --> 00:09:36.033
- If there would have been a
time angled to this problem

00:09:36.033 --> 00:09:39.980
that would have made it much
more simpler for all of us

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.240
because I feel post independence,

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.580
all the governments in this country

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.020
have actually done nothing
good for the majority

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.247
and for the minority.

00:09:50.247 --> 00:09:53.050
On a way, social sense
or economic indicators

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.372
we are not counting in,

00:09:54.372 --> 00:09:57.000
the governments have definitely done,

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.230
that's why we are where we are right now.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.346
- Make no mistake,

00:10:00.346 --> 00:10:02.795
government since 1950s
wouldn't have done anything.

00:10:02.795 --> 00:10:04.013
I agree with you.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.350
But 2014 onwards, we have a government

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:11.660
who has an official policy to
discriminate against Muslims.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.030
We have this Qurbani, the
sacrifice of the animal

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.040
and it takes place at our village.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:19.040
And we go to village
and bring back the meat.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.848
From last two years, we are
not bringing back the meat

00:10:21.848 --> 00:10:23.910
because we believe traveling with the meat

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:24.765
is very dangerous.

00:10:24.765 --> 00:10:28.240
They'll stop you and they'll
lynch you saying that it's cow.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.940
So this government has multiplied hate

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:34.060
and hate crimes exponentially.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.484
It is not something
which is just happening

00:10:35.484 --> 00:10:37.020
and they're hypothetic about it,

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.191
this is their policy.

00:10:38.191 --> 00:10:40.915
And these are seasoned politicians

00:10:40.915 --> 00:10:43.121
making very absurd claims.

00:10:43.121 --> 00:10:44.562
That you should go to Pakistan and all,

00:10:44.562 --> 00:10:47.560
and you and I may think that
they're buffoons and idiots

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.810
but what they're doing actually
is they're normalizing it.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.643
- Yeah.

00:10:51.643 --> 00:10:54.180
- Unlike Congress and
which this politician

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.640
has said it very right,
Congress may be corrupt.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.680
I agree with you, but this government

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:03.590
has overtaken the
institutions so completely.

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:07.490
The judiciary, the investigating agencies,

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.047
- [Both] The media.

00:11:09.047 --> 00:11:11.240
- Yeah.
- So I think-

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.880
- All of that was already taken over on-

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:14.850
- No.
- Not so much.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:18.070
- I think that's living incomplete denial.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.750
Governments before this
must have done this.

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.890
What we are seeing now is a
support towards all of this.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:24.890
- So basically you were-

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:27.119
- They supported
blatantly, it's happening,

00:11:27.119 --> 00:11:29.890
without any regret that they're
violating the constitution.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.296
- So the problem is the degree here-

00:11:31.296 --> 00:11:32.129
- They're violating law.

00:11:32.129 --> 00:11:33.295
There's open support for it.

00:11:33.295 --> 00:11:36.000
When did we see previous
government supporting it?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.080
They at least had the knack and the shame

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.110
to the go ahead and oppose it.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:39.943
Even on the face open.

00:11:39.943 --> 00:11:41.549
Even though you know in your head

00:11:41.549 --> 00:11:44.420
there must have been some
way had a hand in this

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.830
but they never supported it openly.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.970
What we see now is open
blatant, shameless support.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:52.690
And it has led to such violent
situation on the ground.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:53.710
Like he correctly said,

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.110
people are being lynched
for just carrying meat.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:03.030
- I don't think it's the
government who did the lynchings

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.150
and the people who did the lynchings

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:06.690
they have been arrested.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:09.070
And even our prime minister
has said several times

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:12.680
that it has denounced those acts.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.540
So I don't think it's the
government who's not doing,

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.440
it's a law and order issue in UP.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:20.090
And it should be looked at as that.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.100
Secondly, I don't think the government

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.342
is increasing the divide
between Hindus and Muslims.

00:12:24.342 --> 00:12:26.160
I think the divide has always been there

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.223
since the partition.

00:12:28.399 --> 00:12:29.330
Second of all,
- No.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.220
- Speaking to the Ram Mandir issue,

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.253
there my stance is the Muslims have

00:12:32.253 --> 00:12:35.430
thousands of mosques all over the world,

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.593
but Ram was born only at one place.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.360
So I personally believe,

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.400
that the Ram Mandir should have been there

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.580
and the the Supreme court
has given Islamic society

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.133
the right to build a mosque, right beside,

00:12:50.192 --> 00:12:52.610
and it would be like why
would we ever want to take

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:53.780
kardha away from you?

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:54.613
It's like that.

00:12:54.613 --> 00:12:58.270
That place is too special
to us than it is to you.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.003
And just out of magnanimity,

00:13:01.368 --> 00:13:06.150
it would be magnanimous of
the Muslims to just give that.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.582
But I'm not really
emotional about that issue.

00:13:08.582 --> 00:13:09.530
It could have gone either way

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.390
and I would've been fine with it.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.214
- What you're saying is that the Muslims

00:13:13.214 --> 00:13:14.960
should have shown magnanimity,

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.565
is what the general view would have been.

00:13:16.565 --> 00:13:18.514
And the Supreme court has gone by it,

00:13:18.514 --> 00:13:19.762
just because they're minority,

00:13:19.762 --> 00:13:21.203
they're weak, they're less in number,

00:13:21.203 --> 00:13:23.460
let them come forward and show magnanimity

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.020
and to the majority why
should we show magnanimity?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.640
And let's not forget,

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.270
that a mosque did exist at that place

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:31.810
that was demolished.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:34.250
There is proper videographic evidence

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.610
to show that people
were on top of the tomb

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:37.958
and they demolished that mosque.

00:13:37.958 --> 00:13:39.339
And then you say, give it to us,

00:13:39.339 --> 00:13:41.670
give the place to us
because Ram was born here.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:42.503
And let me get

00:13:42.503 --> 00:13:43.336
your facts right.
- And no evidence of that.

00:13:43.336 --> 00:13:45.640
- There has been affidavit
in the Supreme court

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:46.920
by the government itself

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:50.230
stating that there is
no evidence whatsoever.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.690
In fact, by the Archeological
Society of India,

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.640
also that there is no fact whatsoever

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.041
to state and to confirm that Lord Ram

00:13:57.041 --> 00:13:59.040
was actually born at that place.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.370
So your basic foundation
of why the judgment is good

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.020
is flawed in itself.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.360
- So I just never wanted to go

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.701
on this mandir-masjid kind of a thing,

00:14:08.701 --> 00:14:11.810
but I just want to clarify here,

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:15.590
maybe anybody who has done on masjid

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.350
they have destroyed that masjid

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.220
and that is the wrong thing.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:22.560
But do you know how
many temples in Kashmir

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.520
have they burnt, 350 temples?

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.210
- Are we settling scores?
- Exactly.

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.624
That doesn't justify.
- So we should not,

00:14:29.624 --> 00:14:30.734
this is a wrong thing.
- One wrong does not justify

00:14:30.734 --> 00:14:31.890
the other.
- This is a wrong thing,

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.126
wrong statement to say-

00:14:33.126 --> 00:14:33.960
- But you're justifying it.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:34.793
No, so-

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.553
- That intolerance has
been to Muslims only.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.300
- I was at work and the entire debate

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.828
about CAA and NRC was going on

00:14:43.828 --> 00:14:45.390
and working in news means

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:47.980
that's a very big discussion topic.

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.600
If I was to ever voice an opinion

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.088
the immediate rebuttal
it's often said in jest,

00:14:52.088 --> 00:14:54.480
but that doesn't of course make it okay.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.160
Is, oh, why are you bothered?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.241
You can just go back to Pakistan.

00:14:58.241 --> 00:15:00.980
Even though I have
absolutely no affiliation

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.520
but my identity is then
brought into question.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.534
My loyalty towards my country

00:15:04.534 --> 00:15:07.020
is brought into question by these things.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:09.520
It goes back all the way
to middle school as well.

00:15:10.497 --> 00:15:12.860
- [Interviewer] Hindus and Muslims

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.303
can coexist peacefully in India.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:20.673
- Really?

00:15:20.673 --> 00:15:21.954
- Oh my God.
(Pallavi chuckles)

00:15:21.954 --> 00:15:22.787
- Oh God,

00:15:22.787 --> 00:15:23.620
it's just me.
- What is wrong

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.930
with you people?

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:25.940
Of course.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:27.140
You are not born biggit.

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:31.121
You were turned into one,
by all these politicians

00:15:31.121 --> 00:15:33.173
and all the men who wants to
keep their power to themselves

00:15:33.173 --> 00:15:34.510
and don't want to work.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.190
So they need things to divide people.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:39.016
- I think we've been
living fairly peaceful

00:15:39.016 --> 00:15:40.760
to be very honest.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:43.150
There have been some incidences,

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.610
there is obviously been a spike,

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.150
but look at us.

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.470
We are having such a sound conversation

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.740
and there has definitely
been an increament

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:55.830
in the number of interreligious marriages,

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.030
more Muslim scholars being
part of public institutions.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.310
I'm a thorough optimist.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.480
I feel that the trajectory
is definitely going uphill

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.140
despite all the hiccups that we are facing

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.410
at this point in time
for political reasons.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:11.150
- No, I don't agree
that it's going uphill.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:14.390
I think it's getting worse as of now,

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.660
since 2014 like Kabir said.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.600
But I think, yes,

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.410
there's definitely a place to coexist

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.670
because we have been doing that since,

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:22.780
even before independence

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:25.007
- A thousand years.

00:16:25.007 --> 00:16:27.240
- So we have coexisted for so long.

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.750
Also I think the situation on the ground,

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.800
like we are all the privileged
lot, so let's accept that.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.560
But even if you see very common
people on the ground also,

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:38.260
I don't think there is as much as divide

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.270
as being portrayed by the media.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:44.180
And the only reason the
media is portraying it

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.990
is because the government
to its own benefit

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.660
wants to push this narrative

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.620
that there is a Hindu-Muslim divide.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.069
That Muslims have been
the cause of your trouble.

00:16:52.069 --> 00:16:54.840
They were the one whose
needs were always put forth.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.644
And despite being majority,
you were always neglected.

00:16:56.644 --> 00:16:58.990
So now we are going to look after you.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.900
So I think the media's
just running that narrative

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:04.330
full throttle since 2014.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:06.470
And it's just becoming
venomous, like Kabir said

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.863
fascism gets to you very, very slowly.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.673
- I'm not very much comfortable

00:17:11.673 --> 00:17:14.840
when you are saying after
2014 it had happened.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.770
So I don't agree.
- Sure, it's all open.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.673
- I don't agree with you on that thing.

00:17:23.024 --> 00:17:26.210
Muslims and Hindus, if born in India

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.520
can coexist very peacefully

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:32.363
and only we need to leave our extremism.

00:17:33.244 --> 00:17:35.870
So whatever maybe that Hindu extremism

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.770
or the Muslim extremism.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:42.190
Extremism is the main issue,
which should be left behind

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:43.774
- You better defend yourselves.

00:17:43.774 --> 00:17:46.620
(Pallavi chuckles)

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.750
- I think like you said,
it's a very optimistic view.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.160
It's very idealistic.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.840
I want it to happen.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.800
I don't know if that'll happen.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:55.633
You're right,

00:17:55.633 --> 00:17:58.163
we have existed together
for a very long time.

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:01.700
We're barely existing together right now.

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:04.200
When this is not a symbiotic relationship,

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.770
we're not happy together,

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.230
I personally blame it on the old guard.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.991
I think a lot of people have prejudice

00:18:09.991 --> 00:18:11.642
because of the experiences they've had.

00:18:11.642 --> 00:18:14.415
And that's trickling down
to younger generations,

00:18:14.415 --> 00:18:18.450
perhaps not to make it
sound extremely dark,

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.540
but if that generations die out

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.166
and conversations like these continue,

00:18:23.166 --> 00:18:25.010
there could be change.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.225
But again, keeping our privilege in mind,

00:18:27.225 --> 00:18:29.940
these conversations are
just how happening here.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:32.250
I am super afraid of
having these conversations

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.400
outside of this.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.030
I am afraid of backlash.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:36.540
I am afraid of being othered.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:39.480
I am afraid of being told that,

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.380
oh, you know, just go back to Pakistan

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.930
where you belong then,
you'll be comfortable there.

00:18:44.305 --> 00:18:46.360
So I don't know if it's happening outside

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.990
of these sort of-
- It is.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.730
In every educated household-

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.184
- Education is very limited though.

00:18:52.184 --> 00:18:53.017
Again-

00:18:53.017 --> 00:18:54.110
- It's not that limited.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:57.610
Definitely, it's one of the
points that we have to focus on.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.290
- I wanted to make the point out

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:04.203
that why is encourageable
optimism is not misplaced.

00:19:06.028 --> 00:19:08.220
Things are bad right now, of course.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.193
And is there fight
between Muslim and Hindus

00:19:10.193 --> 00:19:11.733
which weren't there earlier?

00:19:12.697 --> 00:19:15.945
Say Muslims came to India say 1000 AD.

00:19:15.945 --> 00:19:18.483
Were there wars before that?
- Of course, yes.

00:19:18.483 --> 00:19:21.520
- Were their Muslims,
when there was Mahabharat?

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.540
Was their discrimination
before Muslims came?

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:24.760
There was a cast system.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.350
There is nothing particular

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.730
about any one particular community.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.773
So Hindus and Muslims are not that,

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.023
unique pair who can never be together.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:38.510
Majority of us agree that
they can live together.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.160
All of us want them to live.
- Absolutely.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.627
- Only difference would be
like, you know how much?

00:19:43.627 --> 00:19:45.310
So I think we should be optimistic.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.700
I implore all of you.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.080
We certainly can live together.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.484
- Oh, you just put our foot here.

00:19:51.484 --> 00:19:53.603
- I will, standing.

00:19:53.603 --> 00:19:55.189
(indistinct)

00:19:55.189 --> 00:19:56.041
(all exclaiming)

00:19:56.041 --> 00:19:58.725
- Making coexist.
(all chuckling)

00:19:58.725 --> 00:20:01.308
(upbeat music)

